T0106 "Loudness: momentary/short-term unimplemented, surround weighting absent"
is CLOSED with a real feature slice, not a no-op.

What changed (library-only, 2 TUs recompiled):
  - src/audio/LoudnessAnalysis.hpp: LoudnessAnalysis gains `maxMomentaryLufs`
    (loudest UNGATED 400 ms block) and `maxShortTermLufs` (loudest UNGATED 3 s
    sliding window = kShortTermSeconds/kStepSeconds = 30 consecutive block
    mean-squares); LoudnessAnalyser gains `kShortTermSeconds = 3.000`; a new
    file-level @section documents M/S and why surround weighting is out of
    scope by design.
  - src/audio/LoudnessAnalysis.cpp: result() computes both as peak-holds over
    the existing blockMeanSquares grid. Silence (z==0) is skipped by the same
    >0 guard the ungated mean uses; a window containing silence is never the
    loudest. Success path guarantees >=1 block above -70 LUFS, so both maxima
    are finite by construction.
  - tests/unit/audio/test_LoudnessAnalysis.cpp: new
    momentaryAndShortTermMaximaAreUngatedPeakHolds() -- steady -20 dBFS-peak
    1 kHz tone pins M and S to the -19.993304 LUFS oracle (M==S==I), and a
    4 s tone + 4 s silence proves M/S are ungated peak-holds (both exceed the
    ungated mean by >1 LU, S<=M, M tracks integrated within 0.25 LU).

Surround weighting (the other half of the title) is intentionally absent, not a
defect: kMaxChannels is 2, AudioFrame is stereo-only, no producer in the tree
can hand this analyser a 5.1 signal (see LoudnessError::UnsupportedChannelCount).
BS.1770 Table 3 coefficients would be unreachable dead code. Documented in the
header rather than implemented.

Verification reality: this is pure offline DSP with no GL, audio-device, real
window, live Suno recon, or credential surface. Sanitizers were NOT run -- a cold
-asan/-tsan build is a full recompile on this box and the change is arithmetic
over an existing std::vector (no new allocation/ownership/threading). No
production consumer of LoudnessAnalyser exists yet, so there is no user-visible
behaviour change and no CHANGELOG entry; this is a measurement-library API
addition owned by the header docs, TODO.md and this log.
